course: dictionary
lesson: 1467
title: Casually: relaxed, or pretending
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Casually means in a relaxed, easy way, without seeming worried or careful. Look at the words around it to see which meaning fits. «She said casually, "Oh, I found your wallet."» The word casually tells you she is treating it as no big deal, so it probably matters to her more than she shows.
explain: Casually can also describe clothes. On a non-uniform day you wear casual clothes: everyday clothes, not smart ones. So casually can describe how someone talks, how they act, or what they wear.
explain: Sometimes casually means without much thought or planning. In «The Mole talked casually of the harvest», the Mole is not making a serious plan. He is chatting in an easy, relaxed way. Swap your meaning into the sentence: "The Mole talked in a relaxed way of the harvest" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Other languages work the same way. In French, «Quel jour sommes-nous ?» means "What day is it?" The full answer is «Nous sommes mardi», but the more casual answer is «On est mardi», a friendlier, everyday way of speaking. When you are not sure, check a dictionary.
fact: Casually means in a relaxed, easy way, without seeming worried or careful.
fact: «Casually» can describe clothes for everyday, not smart wear: casual clothes.
fact: «She said casually» often hints that a character is hiding something or pretending it does not matter.
fact: «Casually mentioned» means spoke about something as if it were not important.
fact: «Casually» can also mean now and then, not regularly or deeply: «casually know someone».
exercise: «He said casually, "I'll see you there," but he had been planning this all week.» What does casually suggest? | He is very worried about the meeting | He is shouting in anger | *He is pretending it does not matter | He is falling asleep
exercise: Which clothes would you wear on a relaxed, non-uniform day? | *Casual clothes | A school uniform | Smart wedding clothes | A deep-sea diving suit
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to casually in «The Mole talked casually of the harvest»? | Carefully | *Relaxed | Angrily | Loudly
test: «Ella casually mentioned that she had moved house.» What does casually mean here? | In a long, serious speech | In a rush, with no time to spare | Very loudly, so everyone heard | *Without making a big deal of it
test: In French, «Quel jour sommes-nous ?» has a full answer and a casual answer. Which is the casual answer? | Je ne sais pas | Mardi est le jour | *On est mardi | Nous sommes mardi
exam: Why might a story say a character «said casually» something? | To show they are shouting at the top of their voice | To show the story is written in French | To show they are wearing a uniform | *To show they are hiding a feeling or pretending it does not matter
